IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja1-part3-div4.l4: Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- LAYER 1, Part 3, Division 4 "Appellate jurisdiction", ss 19 to 22B. The source is a plain-text rendering, not the official text.
-- Every name begins with the section it implements. Imports the keel's `scja-core` only. The Third Schedule (case specified in it) is scja3's: it comes in as the input of seam 3.
-- A judgment the text leaves to the Judge or the court (permission, "special grounds", being "satisfied") is a plain input, never guessed.

§ `Part 3: General Division of High Court (continued)`

§§ `Division 4: Appellate jurisdiction`

§§§ `Section 19: Appellate criminal jurisdiction`

-- The five things s 19 lists, in its paragraphs.
DECLARE `s 19 matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 19(a) an appeal from a District Court or Magistrate's Court`
    `s 19(b) a point of law reserved by a special case submitted by a District Court or Magistrate's Court`
    `s 19(ba) a review of an order of a District Court or Magistrate's Court in extradition proceedings`
    `s 19(c) an appeal from a Family Court when exercising criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 19(d) an appeal from a Youth Court`
    `s 19 another matter`

-- Plain gloss: is the hearing of this matter part of the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division? "consists of": the paragraphs are named, and the section has no "only" (fork F10), so a matter
-- outside them is not decided (NOTHING). Paragraphs (a) and (b) describe the hearing: before one or more Judges according to the law of criminal procedure.
-- src:1675 | 19. The appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division
-- src:1676 | consists of —
-- src:1678 | (a) the hearing of appeals from District Courts or Magistrates’
-- src:1679 | Courts before one or more Judges according to the
-- src:1680 | provisions of the law for the time being in force relating
-- src:1681 | to criminal procedure;
-- src:1683 | (b) the hearing of points of law reserved by special cases
-- src:1684 | submitted by a District Court or Magistrate’s Court before
-- src:1685 | one or more Judges according to the provisions of the law
-- src:1686 | for the time being in force relating to criminal procedure;
-- src:1688 | (ba) the hearing of reviews of the orders of District Courts or
-- src:1689 | Magistrates’ Courts in extradition proceedings;
-- src:1693 | (c) the hearing of appeals from Family Courts when exercising
-- src:1694 | criminal jurisdiction; and
-- src:1696 | (d) the hearing of appeals from Youth Courts.
@ref s 19 (src:1675-1696)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 19 matter` @desc What is being heard: an appeal from a District Court or Magistrate's Court, a point of law reserved by a special case, a review of an order in extradition proceedings, an appeal from a Family Court exercising criminal jurisdiction, an appeal from a Youth Court, or something else?
      `the hearing is before one or more Judges according to the law relating to criminal procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hearing before one or more Judges according to the provisions of the law for the time being in force relating to criminal procedure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 the appellate criminal jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 19(a) an appeal from a District Court or Magistrate's Court` THEN
        IF `the hearing is before one or more Judges according to the law relating to criminal procedure` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before one or more Judges according to the provisions of the law for the time being in force relating to criminal procedure"
    WHEN `s 19(b) a point of law reserved by a special case submitted by a District Court or Magistrate's Court` THEN
        IF `the hearing is before one or more Judges according to the law relating to criminal procedure` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before one or more Judges according to the provisions of the law for the time being in force relating to criminal procedure"
    WHEN `s 19(ba) a review of an order of a District Court or Magistrate's Court in extradition proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 19(c) an appeal from a Family Court when exercising criminal jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 19(d) an appeal from a Youth Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "consists of" the paragraphs (a) to (d), with no "only"

§§§ `Section 20: Appellate civil jurisdiction`

-- Plain gloss: is the hearing of this appeal part of the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division? (a) and (b): from a Family Court, or a District Court or Magistrate's Court, exercising jurisdiction
-- of a quasi-criminal or civil nature; (c) from another tribunal as a written law prescribes. "consists of" again has no "only" (fork F10).
-- src:1702 | 20. The appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists
-- src:1703 | of —
-- src:1705 | (a) the hearing of appeals from Family Courts when exercising
-- src:1706 | jurisdiction of a quasi-criminal or civil nature;
-- src:1708 | (b) the hearing of appeals from District Courts and
-- src:1709 | Magistrates’ Courts when exercising jurisdiction of a
-- src:1710 | quasi-criminal or civil nature; and
-- src:1712 | (c) the hearing of appeals from other tribunals as may from
-- src:1713 | time to time be prescribed by any written law.
@ref s 20 (src:1702-1713)
GIVEN `lower court` IS A Court @desc Which court or tribunal made the decision appealed from?
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding` @desc Is the case civil, quasi-criminal or criminal?
      `a written law prescribes an appeal from this tribunal to the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a tribunal other than a court named in the Act: does a written law prescribe an appeal from it to the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20 the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division consists of hearing the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `lower court` EQUALS `Family Court` AND (nature EQUALS `a civil proceeding` OR nature EQUALS `a quasi-criminal proceeding`) THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        IF (`lower court` EQUALS `District Court` OR `lower court` EQUALS `Magistrate's Court`) AND (nature EQUALS `a civil proceeding` OR nature EQUALS `a quasi-criminal proceeding`) THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        IF `lower court` EQUALS `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` AND `a written law prescribes an appeal from this tribunal to the General Division` THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "consists of" the paragraphs (a) to (c), with no "only"

§§§ `Section 21: Appeals from District and Magistrates' Courts`

-- s 21(1)(a), the money test. The amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter at the hearing in the lower court, excluding interest and costs, must "not exceed" $60,000 or the amount an order under
-- s 21(3) specifies. A case with no amount or value is not decided (K2: the Act does not say what an unvalued case counts as).
-- src:1731 | (a) any case where the amount in dispute, or the value of the
-- src:1732 | subject matter, at the hearing before that District Court or
-- src:1733 | Magistrate’s Court (excluding interest and costs) does not
-- src:1734 | exceed $60,000 or such other amount as may be specified
-- src:1735 | by an order made under subsection (3);
@ref s 21(1)(a) (src:1731-1735)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      `the amount specified by an order under section 21(3)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc If the President has by order under section 21(3) varied the amount, what amount does the order specify?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision's `amount in dispute or value of the subject matter, excluding interest and costs`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the Act does not say what a case with no amount in dispute or value of subject matter counts as
    WHEN JUST amount THEN
        CONSIDER `the amount specified by an order under section 21(3)`
        WHEN JUST sum THEN
            IF amount AT MOST sum THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not exceed $60,000 or such other amount as may be specified by an order made under subsection (3)"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF amount AT MOST `the Act's figure for s 21(1)(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not exceed $60,000"

-- s 21(1). Plain gloss: can the person appeal this District Court or Magistrate's Court decision to the General Division, and does the appeal need permission? "only with the permission" in the cases (a) and (b):
-- in those cases, no permission means no appeal (JUST FALSE), permission means the appeal lies (JUST TRUE). Outside both cases the subsection does not speak (NOTHING). "Subject to the provisions of this Act and any
-- other written law": whether another provision changes the result is for that provision. The Third Schedule's answer is seam 3.
-- src:1719 | 21.—(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act and any other written
-- src:1720 | law, an appeal lies to the General Division from a decision of a
-- src:1721 | District Court or Magistrate’s Court only with the permission of that
-- src:1728 | District Court or Magistrate’s Court or the General Division in the
-- src:1729 | following cases:
-- src:1731 | (a) any case where the amount in dispute, or the value of the
-- src:1732 | subject matter, at the hearing before that District Court or
-- src:1733 | Magistrate’s Court (excluding interest and costs) does not
-- src:1734 | exceed $60,000 or such other amount as may be specified
-- src:1735 | by an order made under subsection (3);
-- src:1737 | (b) any case specified in the Third Schedule.
@ref s 21(1) (src:1719-1737)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      `the amount specified by an order under section 21(3)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `permission has been given by the District Court or Magistrate's Court that made the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the District Court or Magistrate's Court that made the decision given permission to appeal?
      `permission has been given by the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division given permission to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) an appeal lies to the General Division from the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (decision's `made by` EQUALS `District Court` OR decision's `made by` EQUALS `Magistrate's Court`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a decision of a District Court or Magistrate's Court"
        IF `s 21(1) permission is needed to appeal from the decision` decision `the amount specified by an order under section 21(3)` `sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            IF `permission has been given by the District Court or Magistrate's Court that made the decision` OR `permission has been given by the General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an appeal lies to the General Division from a decision of a District Court or Magistrate's Court only with the permission of that District Court or Magistrate's Court or the General Division"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the following cases"; outside (a) and (b) the subsection does not say whether an appeal lies

-- s 21(1), the yes/no twin: does this decision fall in a case in which an appeal needs permission? (a) the money test, (b) the Third Schedule. One limb that is JUST TRUE decides it; if neither is JUST TRUE the
-- subsection is not decided (NOTHING), because the limbs are the only cases the subsection names and the text says nothing of any other.
@ref s 21(1) permission is needed (src:1719-1737)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      `the amount specified by an order under section 21(3)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) permission is needed to appeal from the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 21(1)(a) the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` decision `the amount specified by an order under section 21(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        IF `sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the following cases"

-- s 21(2A). An order of the General Division giving or refusing permission under (1) is final. (2) and (2B) are shown deleted.
-- src:1745 | (2A) An order of the General Division giving or refusing
-- src:1746 | permission under subsection (1) is final.
@ref s 21(2A) (src:1745-1746)
GIVEN `the order is an order of the General Division giving or refusing permission under section 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an order of the General Division giving or refusing permission under section 21(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(2A) the order is final` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order is an order of the General Division giving or refusing permission under section 21(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order of the General Division giving or refusing permission under subsection (1)"

-- s 21(3). The President may, after consulting the Chief Justice, by order in the Gazette, vary the amount mentioned in (1).
-- src:1754 | (3) The President may, after consulting the Chief Justice, by order
-- src:1755 | in the Gazette, vary the amount mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 21(3) (src:1754-1755)
GIVEN `the person is the President` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the order the President?
      `the President has consulted the Chief Justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the President consulted the Chief Justice?
      `the variation is made by order in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the variation made by an order in the Gazette?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3) the President may vary the amount mentioned in section 21(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is the President` AND `the President has consulted the Chief Justice` AND `the variation is made by order in the Gazette` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The President may, after consulting the Chief Justice, by order in the Gazette, vary the amount"

§§§ `Section 22: Powers of rehearing`

-- s 22(1). All appeals to the General Division in its appellate civil jurisdiction are by way of rehearing.
-- src:1759 | 22.—(1) All appeals to the General Division in the exercise of its
-- src:1760 | appellate civil jurisdiction are to be by way of rehearing.
@ref s 22(1) (src:1759-1760)
GIVEN `the appeal is to the General Division in the exercise of its appellate civil jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an appeal to the General Division in the exercise of its appellate civil jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the appeal is by way of rehearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appeal is to the General Division in the exercise of its appellate civil jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All appeals to the General Division in the exercise of its appellate civil jurisdiction"

-- s 22(2). In hearing and deciding an appeal, the General Division has all the powers and duties, as to amendment or otherwise, of the court from which the appeal was brought.
-- src:1764 | (2) In hearing and deciding an appeal, the General Division has all
-- src:1765 | the powers and duties, as to amendment or otherwise, of the court
-- src:1766 | from which the appeal was brought.
@ref s 22(2) (src:1764-1766)
GIVEN `the General Division is hearing and deciding an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division hearing and deciding an appeal?
      `the power or duty is one of the court from which the appeal was brought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power or duty one that the court from which the appeal was brought has?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) the General Division has the power or duty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the General Division is hearing and deciding an appeal` AND `the power or duty is one of the court from which the appeal was brought` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In hearing and deciding an appeal, the General Division has all the powers and duties ... of the court from which the appeal was brought"

-- The four ways s 22(3) lists for receiving further evidence.
DECLARE `s 22(3) manner of receiving further evidence` IS ONE OF
    `s 22(3)(a) by oral examination in court`
    `s 22(3)(b) by affidavit`
    `s 22(3)(c) by deposition taken before an examiner or a commissioner`
    `s 22(3)(d) in any other manner`

-- s 22(3). Plain gloss: may the General Division receive further evidence in this manner? Subject to the provisions of the Act and any other written law, by (a) oral examination, (b) affidavit,
-- (c) deposition before an examiner or commissioner, (d) any other manner the court allows.
-- src:1770 | (3) Subject to the provisions of this Act and any other written law,
-- src:1771 | the General Division may receive further evidence —
-- src:1773 | (a) by oral examination in court;
-- src:1775 | (b) by affidavit;
-- src:1777 | (c) by deposition taken before an examiner or a commissioner;
-- src:1778 | or
-- src:1785 | (d) in any other manner as the court may allow.
@ref s 22(3) (src:1770-1785)
GIVEN manner IS A `s 22(3) manner of receiving further evidence` @desc In what manner would the further evidence be received?
      `the General Division allows the other manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For some other manner: does the General Division allow it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(3) the General Division may receive further evidence in this manner` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `s 22(3)(a) by oral examination in court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 22(3)(b) by affidavit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 22(3)(c) by deposition taken before an examiner or a commissioner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 22(3)(d) in any other manner` THEN
        IF `the General Division allows the other manner` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other manner as the court may allow"

-- s 22(4). Except as provided in (5), further evidence may be given to the General Division "only with the permission of the General Division and on special grounds". Where (5) is met, the whole bar goes
-- (fork F11: "Except as provided in subsection (5)" is read as lifting both limbs of the bar, permission AND special grounds; the other reading keeps the special-grounds limb).
-- src:1789 | (4) Except as provided in subsection (5), such further evidence may
-- src:1790 | be given to the General Division only with the permission of the
-- src:1791 | General Division and on special grounds.
@ref s 22(4) (src:1789-1791)
GIVEN `the matters the evidence relates to occurred on` IS A DATE
      `the date of the decision appealed against` IS A DATE
      `the General Division has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division given permission for the further evidence to be given?
      `there are special grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there special grounds for giving the further evidence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(4) the further evidence may be given to the General Division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 22(5) the further evidence may be given to the General Division without permission` `the matters the evidence relates to occurred on` `the date of the decision appealed against` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the General Division has given permission` AND `there are special grounds` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only with the permission of the General Division and on special grounds"

-- s 22(5), the exception to (4). Further evidence may be given without permission if it relates to matters occurring after the date of the decision appealed against.
-- src:1795 | (5) Such further evidence may be given to the General Division
-- src:1796 | without permission if the evidence relates to matters occurring after
-- src:1797 | the date of the decision appealed against.
@ref s 22(5) (src:1795-1797)
GIVEN `the matters the evidence relates to occurred on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the matters the evidence relates to occur?
      `the date of the decision appealed against` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the decision appealed against made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(5) the further evidence may be given to the General Division without permission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matters the evidence relates to occurred on` GREATER THAN `the date of the decision appealed against` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the evidence relates to matters occurring after the date of the decision appealed against"

-- s 22(6). The General Division may draw any inference of fact, give any judgment and make any order. The sentence names no limit; it sits in a section on appeals (the heading is "Powers of rehearing").
-- src:1801 | (6) The General Division may draw any inference of fact, give any
-- src:1802 | judgment and make any order.
@ref s 22(6) (src:1801-1802)
GIVEN `the General Division is hearing and deciding the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division hearing and deciding the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(6) the General Division may draw the inference, give the judgment or make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the General Division is hearing and deciding the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence says nothing about the General Division's power outside the hearing of an appeal

-- s 22(7). The powers in the section (a) may be exercised in relation to any part of the decision appealed against, including a part the appeal does not relate to; (b) may be exercised in favour of any party
-- to the decision appealed against, including a party who has not appealed.
-- src:1806 | (7) The powers in this section —
-- src:1808 | (a) may be exercised in relation to any part of the decision
-- src:1809 | appealed against, including any part of the decision
-- src:1810 | appealed against to which the appeal does not relate; and
-- src:1812 | (b) may be exercised in favour of any party to the decision
-- src:1813 | appealed against, including any party to the decision
-- src:1814 | appealed against who has not appealed against the
-- src:1815 | decision.
@ref s 22(7) (src:1806-1815)
GIVEN `the power is a power in section 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it one of the powers in section 22?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(7)(a) the power may be exercised in relation to any part of the decision appealed against` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the power is a power in section 22` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The powers in this section"

@ref s 22(7)(b) (src:1812-1815)
GIVEN `the power is a power in section 22` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(7)(b) the power may be exercised in favour of any party to the decision appealed against` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the power is a power in section 22` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The powers in this section"

§§§ `Section 22A: Oral hearing not needed for appellate matters generally`

-- s 22A(2). (1) does not allow any part of a proceeding where oral evidence is given to be conducted without an oral hearing, unless all the parties consent.
-- src:1826 | (2) Subsection (1) does not allow any part of a proceeding where
-- src:1827 | oral evidence is given to be conducted without an oral hearing, unless
-- src:1828 | all the parties consent.
@ref s 22A(2) (src:1826-1828)
GIVEN hearing IS A Hearing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22A(2) section 22A(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT hearing's `oral evidence is given in this part of the hearing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any part of a proceeding where oral evidence is given"
        IF hearing's `all the parties consent` THEN JUST TRUE -- the "unless" is met ("unless all the parties consent"), so (2) no longer denies what (1) allows; this function asks what (1) allows, not whether the court may grant (fork F16)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not allow any part of a proceeding where oral evidence is given ... to be conducted without an oral hearing, unless all the parties consent"

-- s 22A(1). Plain gloss: may the General Division decide this matter, in its appellate civil jurisdiction, without hearing oral arguments? Not a matter prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules
-- ("other than": read as the text's no, question QE; fork F6). Subject to (2): where oral evidence is given in a part, (2) applies.
-- src:1821 | 22A.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), the General Division may
-- src:1822 | decide any matter in its appellate civil jurisdiction without hearing
-- src:1823 | oral arguments, other than a matter prescribed by the Rules of Court
-- src:1824 | or the Family Justice Rules.
@ref s 22A(1) (src:1821-1824)
GIVEN `the matter is in the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter within the General Division's appellate civil jurisdiction?
      `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules prescribe as needing oral arguments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22A(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the matter is in the appellate civil jurisdiction of the General Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any matter in its appellate civil jurisdiction"
        IF `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a matter prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 22A(3). In any matter that the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments, it may direct that the matter be heard asynchronously by exchange of written correspondence, subject to (4).
-- src:1830 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), the General Division may, in any
-- src:1831 | matter that the General Division may decide without hearing oral
-- src:1832 | arguments, direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner
-- src:1833 | by exchange of written correspondence with the party or parties using
-- src:1834 | such means of communication as directed by the General Division.
@ref s 22A(3) (src:1830-1834)
GIVEN `the matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22A(3) the General Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any matter that the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments"

-- s 22A(4). The General Division must not hear a matter asynchronously if that would be inconsistent with its duty to ensure the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties.
-- src:1841 | (4) The General Division must not hear a matter in an asynchronous
-- src:1842 | manner if to do so would be inconsistent with the court’s duty to
-- src:1843 | ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties.
@ref s 22A(4) (src:1841-1843)
GIVEN `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would hearing the matter in an asynchronous manner be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22A(4) the General Division must not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty"

-- s 22A(4) as a regulative rule (ruling N2: derived from the decision above). The bearer is "the General Division"; no time is stated.
DECLARE `s 22A(4) party` IS ONE OF `s 22A(4) the General Division`
DECLARE `s 22A(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 22A(4) hears the matter in an asynchronous manner`
    `s 22A(4) takes some other step in the matter`

@ref s 22A(4) must not hear a matter in an asynchronous manner (src:1841-1843)
GIVEN `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 22A(4) party` `s 22A(4) act`
`s 22A(4) the General Division shall not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` MEANS
    IF `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties`
    THEN PARTY `s 22A(4) the General Division`
         SHANT `s 22A(4) hears the matter in an asynchronous manner`
         WITHIN 1
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 22A(4): the General Division heard the matter in an asynchronous manner when to do so was inconsistent with its duty to ensure fairness to all parties"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 22A(5). To avoid doubt, s 22A does not affect the General Division's power to hear oral arguments before deciding a matter that may be decided without them.
-- src:1845 | (5) To avoid doubt, this section does not affect the power of the
-- src:1846 | General Division to hear oral arguments before deciding any matter
-- src:1847 | that may be decided without hearing oral arguments.
@ref s 22A(5) (src:1845-1847)
GIVEN `the matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22A(5) section 22A affects the General Division's power to hear oral arguments before deciding the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section does not affect the power of the General Division to hear oral arguments"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any matter that may be decided without hearing oral arguments"

§§§ `Section 22B: Summary dismissal of certain appeals`

-- s 22B(3). In s 22B, "appeal" includes part of an appeal.
-- src:1877 | (3) In this section, “appeal” includes part of an appeal.
@ref s 22B(3) (src:1877)
GIVEN `it is an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an appeal?
      `it is part of an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it part of an appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22B(3) the thing is an appeal for the purposes of section 22B` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is part of an appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section, “appeal” includes part of an appeal"

-- s 22B(1). Plain gloss: may the General Division, on its own motion, summarily dismiss this appeal in its appellate civil jurisdiction? Only if it is satisfied of (a), (b) or (c). Its satisfaction is the
-- court's judgment, asked as a fact. Limb (b) is the ground shared with ss 17C(1)(a), 38(1)(b) and 56(1)(b) (PLAN.md difficulty 7); its input is this section's own.
-- src:1853 | 22B.—(1) The General Division may, on its own motion,
-- src:1854 | summarily dismiss any appeal to the General Division in the
-- src:1855 | exercise of its appellate civil jurisdiction, if it is satisfied of any of
-- src:1856 | the following:
-- src:1858 | (a) it does not have the jurisdiction to hear and determine the
-- src:1859 | appeal;
-- src:1861 | (b) every issue in the appeal has already been decided by the
-- src:1862 | General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of
-- src:1863 | Appeal in an earlier matter in which the appellant was
-- src:1864 | involved, and the appeal therefore has no merit;
-- src:1866 | (c) such conditions as may be prescribed by the Rules of Court
-- src:1867 | or the Family Justice Rules are met.
@ref s 22B(1) (src:1853-1867)
GIVEN `the appeal is to the General Division in the exercise of its appellate civil jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 22B(1)(a) the General Division does not have the jurisdiction to hear and determine the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division satisfied that it does not have the jurisdiction to hear and determine the appeal?
      `s 22B(1)(b) every issue in the appeal has already been decided in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and the appeal therefore has no merit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division satisfied that every issue in the appeal has already been decided by the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and that the appeal therefore has no merit?
      `s 22B(1)(c) the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division satisfied that the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22B(1) the General Division may on its own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appeal is to the General Division in the exercise of its appellate civil jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any appeal to the General Division in the exercise of its appellate civil jurisdiction"
        IF `s 22B(1)(a) the General Division does not have the jurisdiction to hear and determine the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 22B(1)(b) every issue in the appeal has already been decided in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and the appeal therefore has no merit` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 22B(1)(c) the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are met` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is satisfied of any of the following"

-- s 22B(2). Before summarily dismissing an appeal, the General Division must (a) give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause and (b) consider the appellant's representations.
-- A bare "must" not done answers NOTHING for the dismissal: the text states a duty and does not say what follows (question QB; fork F7).
-- src:1869 | (2) Before summarily dismissing any appeal under subsection (1),
-- src:1870 | the General Division must —
-- src:1872 | (a) give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause
-- src:1873 | why the appeal should not be summarily dismissed; and
-- src:1875 | (b) consider any representations made by the appellant.
@ref s 22B(2) (src:1869-1875)
GIVEN `the appellant was given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why the appeal should not be summarily dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why your appeal should not be summarily dismissed?
      `the General Division considered the representations of the appellant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the General Division consider your representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22B(2) the General Division may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 22B(1) now, as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appellant was given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why the appeal should not be summarily dismissed` AND `the General Division considered the representations of the appellant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Before summarily dismissing any appeal under subsection (1), the General Division must (a) ... and (b) ..." states a duty and does not say what follows if it is not done (fork F7)

-- s 22B(2) as a regulative rule (ruling N2: derived from the decision above). The bearer is "the General Division"; no time is stated.
DECLARE `s 22B(2) party` IS ONE OF `s 22B(2) the General Division`
DECLARE `s 22B(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 22B(2) gives the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause`
    `s 22B(2) considers the representations of the appellant`

@ref s 22B(2)(a) give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause (src:1869-1875)
GIVEN `the General Division is about to summarily dismiss the appeal under section 22B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 22B(2) party` `s 22B(2) act`
`s 22B(2) the General Division must give the appellant an opportunity to show cause and consider the representations` MEANS
    IF `the General Division is about to summarily dismiss the appeal under section 22B(1)`
    THEN PARTY `s 22B(2) the General Division`
         MUST `s 22B(2) gives the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause`
         HENCE PARTY `s 22B(2) the General Division`
               MUST `s 22B(2) considers the representations of the appellant`
               HENCE FULFILLED
               LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 22B(2)(b): the General Division must consider the representations of the appellant"
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 22B(2)(a): the General Division must give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause"
    ELSE FULFILLED
